    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but isn't there a point where \"nuance\" just becomes an excuse to avoid the uncomfortable stuff? like, if we're being truly \"accurate\" and \"critical,\" shouldn't the focus naturally shift toward the systemic issues, since those are the things that shaped the world we live in today? it feels like focusing too much on \"triumphs\" is just a way to sanitize history to make people feel better, rather than actually teaching them how society works.",
