      "content": "You raise an important point. If a curriculum overly emphasizes triumphs without a critical lens casting systemic issues, it can indeed result in a sanitized version of history that fails to prepare students for the challenges of the present and future. It is vital for a history education to be both truthful and critical, ensuring that students understand the full context of events, including the power dynamics and injustices that have shaped society. Striking the right balance requires thoughtfully integrating these elements to present a comprehensive and honest narrative that includes hard truths as well as progress, thus fostering informed and empathetic future citizens.",
